cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this package, please cite it as below.
type: software
title: "Replication package: Screening beats ranking — the value of five copy-trading decisions on a perpetual futures exchange"
abstract: >-
  Code, data and run records for a study measuring what each of the five
  decisions in copy trading is worth, on a panel of 1,928 Hyperliquid accounts
  drawn from a public snapshot of 47,195 addresses, net of cost and over a grid
  of cost levels. Every number in the manuscript is generated from the run
  records; a number typed by hand fails the build.
